+
+`CollectMatching` applies its optional predicate directly to each borrowed
+frame view. The predicate must not mutate or retain that view. Matching frames
+are copied into owned storage before the next `Next` call, preserving nil and
+non-nil empty frames. A nil predicate keeps every frame. On a source error, the
+function returns the frames accepted so far and preserves the original error.
